       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          TCDLYABS.
       AUTHOR.              J M HERTZIG.
       DATE-WRITTEN.        3/7/79.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *SECURITY.
      *
      *REMARKS. THIS IS THE ABSTRACT AND LIST OF DAILY ACTIVITY
      *           ON STORES DATABASE.
      *     DEC. 28, 1981
      *       1. MODIFIED LOGIC TO PRINT WITHDRAWALS AND RETURNS
      *          TOGETHER SORTED BY DEPT. CHARGED. RETURNS WILL SHOW
      *          A NEGATIVE AMT. CHARGED.
      *              KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *      ON FEBRUARY 23, 1982, ADDED DDAILY-TC-CODES OF 350 AND 351.
      *      TRANSACTION CODE 350 IS TO REPLACE TRANSACTION CODE 326...
      *      WHICH IS THE ADDITION OF FREIGHT INFORMATION.  TRANSACTION
      *      CODE 351 IS THE MODIFICATION OF FREIGHT INFORMATION.  LMB.
      *
      *      IN APRIL, 1982, THIS PROGRAM WAS CHANGED TO UPDATE A KSAM
      *      FILE OF MONTHLY USAGE.  USAGE IN THE KSAM FILE "USAGEFIL"
      *      IS UPDATED FOR ISSUES, RETURNS, OR ADJUSTMENTS. (FOR
      *      ISSUES OR ADJUSTMENTS DOWN, A NEGATIVE NUMBER IS ADDED
      *      TO THE USAGE FIGURE).
      *        THE KSAM FILE HAS 15 FIELDS WHICH LOOK LIKE THIS -
      *
      *    : CODE : JAN : FEB : MAR : .... : DEC : CURRENT : YEST :
      *
      *    THIS PROGRAM UPDATES ONLY THE "CURRENT" AND "YEST" FIELDS.
      *    IN THE CUTTOFF JOB STREAM, A PRE-PROCCESSING PROGRAM CALLED
      *    "XUSEUPDT" MOVE ZEROS TO EVERY "YEST" FIELD.  IF NEW
      *    NEW MONTH, IT MOVES "CURRENT" TO ONE OF THE MONTH FIELDS,
      *    AND MOVES ZERO TO "CURRENT". CIH.
      *
      *
      *    ON APRIL 19, 1982
      *         ADDED A NEW TC CODE 334 WHICH IS A CODE TRANSFER
      *             KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 20,1982
      *         ADDED LOGIC TO PUT OUT A HEADER TC (001) IN THE FORM
      *          'YYMMDDHHMMSS001PLT' AND TO PUT A SEQ CTR ON THE
      *         EXISING (900) TC AFTER THE RCD CTR. THIS SEQ CTR WILL
      *         BE KEPT IN MPLTINFO AND IS FOUND BY USING 'P 02' AS
      *         THE SEARCH KEY THIS SEQ CTR WILL BE INCREMENTED BY 1
      *         EACH TIME CUTOFF IS RAN AND WILL BE COMPARED TO THE
      *         SEQ CTR ON THE IBM SIDE TO MAKE SURE THE CORRECT
      *         ABSTFILE WAS SENT.
      *             KURT MOVSESIAN.
      *
      *    ON JUNE 14, 1982, ADDED TWO NEW TRANSACTION CODES FOR
      *    ALL C-ORDERS WHOSE ORDERED UM IS DIFFERENT FROM THE PRICE
      *    UM.  TC 327 PUTS OUT THE QUANTITY IN THE PRICE UM.  TC
      *    328 IS A CORRECTION TO TC 327.   LMB.
      *
      *    ON JULY 29, 1982  ADDED TWO NEW TRANSACTION CODES FOR
      *    FREIGHT INFORMATION.  TRANSACTION CODE 352 IS FOR ADDITIONAL
      *    FREIGHT INFORMATION; AND TRANSACTION CODE 353 IS THE COR-
      *    RECTION TO THE 352 TRANSACTION.  LMB.
      *
      *    IN AUGUST, 1982, CHANGED THIS PGM FOR AKRON.  IF AKRON, IF
      *    NEW MONTH, ONLY RAW MATERIAL ISSUES, RETURNS, OR ADJUSTMENTS
      *    ARE SENT, OTHER TRANSACTIONS ARE HELD BACK FOR NEXT CUTOFF.
      *    THIS IS TO HELP AKRON ACCOUNTING GET A CLEAN MONTH END
      *    CUTTOFF (BECAUSE THERE IS A 1-DAY LAG IN RAW MATERIAL
      *    TRANSACTIONS FROM THE BANBURY EXPLOSION.  CIH.
      *
      *    IN OCTOBER, 1982, ADDED NON-STOREROOM RECEIPTS AND NON-STR
      *    PURCHASE ORDER ITEMS TO REPORT.  FOR RECEIPTS, SEPERATED
      *    RECEIPTS AND RECEIPT CORRECTIONS.  FOR PURCHASE ORDER ITEMS,
      *    SEPERATED PO ITEMS AND PO ITEM CORRECTIONS.  (THESE WERE
      *    PREVIOUSLY UNDER THE SAME HEADING, "DAILY STOREROOM PURCHASE
      *    ORDERS").  CIH.
      *
      *    IN NOVEMBER, 1982, MADE SEVERAL CHANGES.
      *    1.  COMBINED AKRON & PLANT VERSIONS INTO 1 PGM.  THERE ARE
      *        NOW 2 PRINT FILES, ONE WITH FORMS CONTROL AND 1 WITHOUT,
      *        SO THAT AKRON WILL HAVE NO REPLY'S TO FORMS.
      *    2.  PUT THE DELETES OF DDAILYTC AFTER ABSTFILE IS CLOSED,
      *        INSTEAD OF DELETEING AS ABSTFILE IS WRITTEN.  THIS IS
      *        SO THAT IF THERE IS A SYSTEM FAILURE DURING INPUT
      *        (ABSTFILE WOULD BE LOST), DDAILYTC WILL STILL BE THERE.
      *    3.  PUT UPDATES OF USAGEFILE IN INPUT SECTION INSTEAD OF
      *        OUTPUT SECTION.
      *    4.  WRITE A FILE TELLING WHICH CODES HAD USAGE UPDATED.
      *        THIS TELLS "XUSUPDT" WHICH CODES NEED 0 MOVED TO
      *        "USED YESTERDAY" IN THE NEXT CUTOFF.
      *    5.  ADDED DISPLAYS WHICH WILL SHOW UP IN THE JOB STREAM
      *        OUTPUT.  IN CASE OF PROBLEMS, THESE DISPLAYS WILL TELL
      *        HOW FAR CUTTOFF GOT BEFORE IT CRASHED.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 25, 1983, ADDED A HIGH USAGE TRANSACTION OF 399.
      *    THE PROGRAM WILL ALSO PRINT OUT THE HIGH USAGE INFORMA-
      *    TION.  LMB.
      *
      *    ON APRIL 27, 1983, CHANGED THE USAGE UPDATE PROCEDURE.
      *    BEFORE, WE PUT ALL USAGE IN THE MONTH-TO-DATE AREA AND MOVED
      *    THIS TO THE CORRESPONDING MONTH AT THE START OF A NEW MONTH.
      *    THIS CAN CAUSE INACCURACIES UNLESS THE CUTTOFF IS RUN AT
      *    EXACTLY 12:00 MIDNIGHT, BECAUSE TRANSACTIONS AFTER THE
      *    CUTOFF BUT BEFORE THE NEW MONTH END UP IN THE WRONG MONTH
      *    USAGE FIGURE.  WILL CORRECT THIS BY GOING BY THE TRANSACTION
      *    DATE IF THE MONTH IS DIFFERENT FROM THE CURRENT MONTH.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON JUNE 23, 1983, ADDED TWO NEW TRANSACTIONS.
      *      -335  DISPERSAL TO OUTSIDE OF PLANT
      *      -336  RECEIPT FROM OUTSIDE OF PLANT
      *    THESE TRANSACTIONS WILL BE CREATED BY "XTRANS.OBJECT".
      *    CIH.
      *
      *    ON OCTOBER 5, 1983, CHANGED THE "FIRST WORK DAY OF NEW MONTH"
      *    PROCEDURE FOR AKRON.  FROM NOW ON, WE WILL LET CERTAIN
      *    TRANSACTIONS GO THROUGH ON 1ST DAY OF MONTH REGARDLESS OF WHAT
      *    PLANT IN AKRON.  THESE TRANSACTIONS ARE:  320, 321, 322, 323,
      *    324, 32D, 350, 351, 352, 353, 360, 361, 370, AND 371.  CIH
      *
      *
      *    ON DECEMBER 5, 1983, CHANGED THE DELETE TO DDAILYTC LOGIC.
      *    THE OLD LOGIC DID A BACKWARD SERIAL READ OF DDAILYTC.  THIS
      *    CAUSED SOME PROBLEMS, SO CHANGED LOGIC TO FIRST REWIND THE
      *    DATA SET ("DBCLOSE" MODE 3), THEN DO A FORWARD SERIAL
      *    READ.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON DECEMBER 6, 1983, RAN INTO A PROBLEM WITH USAGE
      *    UPDATES THAT OCCURS WHEN A TRANSACTION COMES THROUGH FOR
      *    A CODE THAT HAS BEEN PREVIOUSLY DELETED OFF THE SYSTEM.
      *    IN THIS CASE THE PROGRAM BLOWS UP IN THE USAGE UPDATE
      *    LOOP.  IN ORDER TO PREVENT THIS IN CASE OF A SIMILAR
      *    EVENT, THE "CKREADBYKEY" CHECKS FOR A KSAM STATUS OF
      *    23 (KEY DOES NOT EXIST).  IF SO, IT DISPLAYS AN ERROR
      *    MESSAGE TO THE JOB STREAM AND CONTINUES.  ANY KSAM
      *    STATUS OTHER THAN 23 OR 0 IS STILL CONSIDERED A FATAL
      *    ERROR.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON DECEMBER 28, 1983, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *       1.  ADDED A COUNT OF TRANSACTIONS 333 (WITHDRAWAL),
      *           330 (RETURN), AND 323 (RECEIPTS AT DOCK).  THESE
      *           COUNTS ARE PRINTED ON THE LAST PAGE.
      *       2.  TOOK OUT "PRINT-FILE2", THE NON-FORMS REPLY
      *           PRINT FILE.  NOW, INSTEAD, IF FORMS REPLYS ARE
      *           WANTED, A FILE STATEMENT IN THE JOB STREAM WILL
      *           BE USED.  THIS FILE STATEMENT IS IN THE FORM
      *           FILE PRNT1;FORMS="CUTOFF FORM".
      *       3.  FIXED A BUG IN WHICH ANY STOREROOM RECEIPTS WITH
      *           A PARTIALLY ALPHABETIC CORP CODE GREATER THAN
      *           "NON-STR" SHOWED UP AS AN INVALID TRANSACTION.
      *           CIH.
      *
      *    ON AUGUST 8, 1984, CHANGED THE "NEW MONTH" DETERMINATION
      *    FROM THE "00000000" RECORD IN USAGEFIL TO THE JCW
      *    "MONTHEND".  THIS JCW IS SET BY THE PROGRAM "XUSEUPDT"
      *    WHICH RUNS BEFORE THIS PROGRAM.  THE JCW IS NOW USED
      *    SO THAT IT CAN KEY ANOTHER STEP IN THE "BCUTOFF" JOB
      *    TO STREAM A SPECIAL AVERAGE USAGE UPDATE JOB AFTER
      *    THE ACTUAL "CUTOFF" (XCDLYABS) IS DONE - SO THAT USERS
      *    WILL BE ABLE TO SIGN ON WHILE THE JOB IS RUNNING.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON NOV 14, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *       1.  TOOK OUT ALL PRINT LOGIC FOR THE DAILY ACTIVITY
      *           REPORT.  ALL PRINTING OF DAILY ACTIVITY IS NOW
      *           HANDLED BY THE SUBPROGRAM "TCDLYAB2".  IN THIS WAY,
      *           ONLY 1 PROGRAM NEED BE CHANGED WHEN CHANGES TO
      *           THE REPORT ARE NEEDED (IE, ADDING TRANSACTION CODES).
      *           PREVIOUSLY, BOTH TCDLYABS AND TCDLYAB2 HAD TO BE
      *           CHANGED, WHICH RESULTED IN SOME MINOR DIFFERENCES
      *           BETWEEN THE TWO REPORTS. "TCDLYAB2" HAS BEEN CHANGED
      *           TO BE ABLE TO PRINT ANY OF THE FILES "ABSTFILE",
      *           "ABSTFIL2" THRU "ABSTFIL5", BASED ON A PARAMETER
      *           PASSED THRU THE JOB STREAM (READ BY A COBOL
      *           ACCEPT STATEMENT). A PARAMETER CARD TO PASS TO
      *           THE REPORT MUST THEREFORE BE ADDED TO THE
      *           "BCUTOFF" JOB STREAM, DIRECTLY AFTER THE ":RUN
      *           XCDLYABS" CARD.
      *       2.  CHANGED THE "MONTH END LOGIC" - SPECIAL CUTOFF
      *           PROCEDURE FOR THE FIRST WORKING DAY OF EACH MONTH.
      *           THE OLD LOGIC WORKED AS FOLLOWS:
      *             1.  SPECIAL NEW MONTH PROCEDURE WAS DONE ONLY FOR
      *                 AKRON PLANTS.
      *             2.  ON THE FIRST DAY OF THE MONTH, ALL ISSUES, RETURNS,
      *                 AND ADJUSTMENTS WERE HELD BACK, EXCEPT FOR ISSUES,
      *                 RETURNS, AND ADJUSTMENTS FROM THE MIX CENTER IN
      *                 AKRON.  IT WAS ASSUMED THESE ISSUES WERE THE RESULT
      *                 OF BANBURY EXPLOSION TRANSACTIONS, AND THUS WERE
      *                 FROM THE PREVIOUS MONTH.
      *                 THE INTENT WAS TO ACTUALLY LET THRU ONLY
      *                 TRANSACTIONS FOR THE PREVIOUS MONTH, AS ASKED FOR
      *                 BY AKRON ACCOUNTING TO FACILITATE MONTH-END
      *                 PROCESSING.
      *             3.  CERTAIN TRANSACTIONS WERE LET THRU REGARDLESS OF
      *                 NEW MONTH, SINCE THEY DID NOT AFFECT MONTH END
      *                 PROCESSING.  THESE INCLUDED PO ITEM CREATION AND
      *                 MODIFICATION, DOCK RECEIPTS AND MODIFICATIONS,
      *                 ETC.
      *
      *          THE NEW LOGIC WORKS AS FOLLOWS:
      *             1.  ANY PLANT MAY EXECUTE THE NEW-MONTH PROCEDURE.
      *                 THIS IS DETERMINED BY HAVING THE KEY "NM01"
      *                 IN THE "MPLTINFO" DATA SET.  IF THE KEY IS NOT
      *                 THERE, THE NEW MONTH LOGIC IS NEVER EXECUTED.
      *             2.  THE CUTOFF CRITERIA IS NOW SOLELY THE DATE STAMP
      *                 ON THE TRANSACTION.  IF IT IS THE FIRST WORKING
      *                 DAY OF THE MONTH, AND IT IS A PLANT WITH THE
      *                 "NM01" KEY, THEN ONLY TRANSACTIONS FROM THE
      *                 PREVIOUS MONTH ARE LET THRU.  ALL TRANSACTIONS
      *                 FROM THE CURRENT MONTH ARE HELD BACK, AGAIN TO
      *                 FACILITATE MONTH-END PROCESSING BY ACCOUNTING
      *                 PROGRAMS.
      *             3.  TRANSACTIONS NOT AFFECTING INVENTORY (DOCK
      *                 RECEIPTS, ETC) ARE STILL LET THRU REGARDLESS.
      *             4.  FOR BANBURY TRANSACTION, THE PRODUCTION DATE
      *                 (THE DATE MATERIAL WAS ACTUALLY "ISSUED") IS
      *                 USED RATHER THAN THE TRANSACTION DATE (THE DATE
      *                 THOSE TRANSACTIONS REACHED THE HP SYSTEM -
      *                 NORMALLY A 1 DAY DELAY).
      *             5.  FOR CORRECTIONS TO BANBURY TRANSACTIONS, FORMERLY
      *                 DONE BY ISSUING OR RETURNING THE MATERIAL, A
      *                 NEW PROGRAM IS INSTITUTED.  THIS PROGRAM REQUIRES
      *                 THAT A PRODUCTION DATE BE SPECIFIED - THE ACTUAL
      *                 USAGE DATE OF BANBURY TRANSACTIONS THAT ARE
      *                 BEING CORRECTED.  THIS PRODUCTION DATE WILL AGAIN
      *                 BE USED AS THE DATE STAMP FOR NEW MONTH PROCESSING.
      *             6.  USAGE WILL BE UPDATED BY THE PRODUCTION DATE STAMP
      *                 FOR BANBURY TRANSACTIONS, RATHER THAN BY
      *                 TRANSACTION DATE.  IN THIS WAY, THE USAGE AS
      *                 RECORDED BY ACCOUNTING PROGRAMS FOR EACH MONTH
      *                 SHOULD MATCH THE USAGE FIGURES HELD ON THE HP
      *                 SYSTEM.
      *
      *         15MAY92 - SPECIAL NOTE ON USE OF THE NEW-MONTH
      *                   INDICATOR (KEY NM01 IN MPLTINFO) ---DAVE PLUM
      *
      *                 W A R N I N G - WHEN BOTH THE NEW-MONTH
      *                 INDICATOR (KEY NM01) AND THE TC-999 INDICATOR
      *                 (KEY TC99) ARE BOTH IN PLACE AND NEW-MONTH
      *                 PROCESSING IS BEING EXECUTED, TC-999 RECORDS
      *                 MAY BE CREATED WHOSE ONHAND VALUES
      *                 "INCORRECTLY" REFLECT SOME NEW-MONTH BUSINESS.
      *
      *                 HERE IS AN EXAMPLE:
      *                  - NM01 KEY IS IN PLACE TO SIGNIFY A
      *                    "NEW-MONTH" PLANT
      *                  - TC99 KEY IS IN PLACE TO SIGNIFY THAT TC 999
      *                    RECORDS SHOULD BE CREATED
      *
      *                 CONSIDER THE FOLLOWING ACITIVITY FOR CODE
      *                 1234567
      *                  - AN ISSUE OF 2 UNITS ON 04/30/92 AT 16:00:00
      *                    RESULTS IN AN ONHAND VALUE OF 10 EA
      *                  - AT 6 PM ON 04/30/92 THIS PROGRAM IS EXECUTED
      *                    AND THE FOLLOWING TRANSACTIONS ARE INCLUDED
      *                    IN THE ABSTFILE
      *                      1) 04/30/92 16:00:00 ISSUE (TC 333) OF
      *                         2 UNITS
      *                      2) 04/30/92 16:00:00 TC 999 WITH FINAL
      *                         ONHAND = 10
      *                  - AN ISSUE OF 5 UNITS ON 04/30/92 AT 20:00:00,
      *                    ONHAND=5
      *                  - AN ISSUE OF 3 UNITS ON 05/01/92 AT 08:00:00,
      *                    ONHAND=2
      *                  - AT 6 PM ON 05/01/92 THIS PROGRAM IS EXECUTED
      *                    AND "NEW-MONTH" PROCESSING IS PERFORMED.
      *                    THE FOLLOWING RECORDS ARE INCLUDED IN THE
      *                    ABSTFILES
      *                      1) 04/30/92 20:00:00 ISSUE (TC 333) OF
      *                         5 UNITS
      *                      2) 04/30/92 20:00:00 TC 999 WITH FINAL
      *                         ONHAND=2
      *                          * THIS PGM WOULD EXCLUDE THE ISSUE
      *                            DATED 05/01/92 FROM THE ABSTFILE,
      *                            BUT THE ISSUE FROM 04/30/92
      *                            20:00:00 WOULD TRIGGER THE PROGRAM
      *                            TO OBTAIN THE ONHAND VALUE FROM
      *                            MSTORERM AS OF 6 PM ON 05/01/92 AND
      *                            IT IS 2 EA.
      *
      *                  THIS TYPE OF "ERROR" CAUSED NUMEROUS PROBLEMS
      *                  WITH AKRON STORES ACCOUNTING (A2520), SINCE
      *                  OUR FINAL ONHAND VALUES FOR THE MONTH
      *                  INCLUDED TRANSACTIONS WHICH WERE ASSIGNED TO
      *                  THE NEW-MONTH.  MOST ERRORS TENDED TO REVERSE
      *                  THEMSELVES AND DISAPEER THE NEXT MONTH, BUT
      *                  THERE WAS GREAT CONFUSION.
      *
      *                  IN FACT, THE NM01 KEY WAS REMOVED FROM THE
      *                  AKRON PLANTS' DATABASES IN MAY 1992.
      *
      *
      *    ON DEC 4, 1984, FIXED A BUG CREATED BY THE PREVIOUS CHANGES.
      *    THIS BUG CAUSED THE BEGINNING AND ENDING CONTROL RECORD DATES
      *    TO BE DIFFERENT, RESULTING IN THE SEND BEING REJECTED BY THE
      *    MAINFRAME PROGRAM.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON MARCH 2, 1985, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *      1.  ADDED THE TRANSACTION TYPE "999" TO THE PROGRAM.  THIS
      *      TRANSACTION PASSES THE ONHAND OF ANY CORPORATE CODE THAT
      *      HAD ACTIVITY ON THAT DAY.  ONLY ONE "999" TRANSACTION
      *      IS GENERATED FOR ANY CODE THAT HAD ACTIVITY, EVEN THOUGH
      *      THERE MAY HAVE BEEN MULTIPLE TRANSACTIONS FOR ANY CODE.
      *      THIS IS ACCOMPLISHED BY USING A SORT FILE AND ELIMINATING
      *      DUPLICATES (USING ONLY THE LATEST TRANSACTION FOR A CODE).
      *      THE "999" TRANSACTIONS WILL FOLLOW THE LAST ACTUAL
      *      TRANSACTION IN "ABSTFILE", BUT COME IMMEDIATELY BEFORE
      *      THE FINAL CONTROL RECORD IN THE FILE.  THESE TRANSACTIONS
      *      WILL BE GENERATED FOR A PLANT ONLY IF THE "TC99" KEY IS
      *      FOUND IN THAT PLANT'S DATABASE.  IN THIS WAY, THE PROGRAM
      *      WILL BE FLEXIBLE ENOUGH TO PROVIDE THE "999" TRANSACTION
      *      FEATURE TO ONLY THOSE PLANTS THAT WISH TO USE IT.
      *      (THE "999" TRANSACTIONS WERE DESIGNED PRIMARILY TO SOLVE
      *      ONHAND DIFFERENCE PROBLEMS AT KELLY PLANTS BETWEEN THE
      *      HP SYSTEM AND THE PRAPS SYSTEM).
      *      2.  CHANGED THE LOCKING LOGIC.  FORMERLY, THE DATASET
      *      "DDAILYTC" (TRANSACTION DATA SET) WAS LOCKED DURING THE
      *      CUTOFF PROCEDURE.  NOW THE ENTIRE DATABASE MUST BE LOCKED
      *      TO PROVIDE INTEGRITY FOR THE "999" TRANSACTIONS.  THIS
      *      DATA INTEGRITY WOULD BE LOST UNDER THE OLD LOCKING METHOD
      *      AS IN THE FOLLOWING EXAMPLE:
      *        1.  AN STOREROOM ISSUE IS DONE, AND UPDATES THE ONHAND
      *            VALUE IN THE "MSTORERM" DATASET.
      *        2.  BEFORE THE ISSUE PROGRAM CREATES THE TRANSACTION IN
      *            THE "DDAILYTC" DATASET, "CUTOFF" (THIS PROGRAM)
      *            LOCKS "DDAILYTC" AND STARTS THE CUTOFF PROCEDURE.
      *        3.  A "DBGET" IS DONE TO "MSTORERM" TO GET THE ONHAND
      *            VALUE FOR SOME OTHER TRANSACTION FOR THE SAME CODE
      *            AS THE ISSUE TRANSACTION IN "1".
      *         4.  THE "999" TRANSACTION IS CREATED WITH THE VALUE
      *             OBTAINED IN "3".  HOWEVER, THIS VALUE IS INCORRECT,
      *             BECAUSE THE ISSUE TRANSACTION IN "1" WILL NOT BE
      *             SENT UNTIL THE NEXT DAY, BUT THE ONHAND IN THE
      *             "999" TRANS ALREADY REFLECTS THAT ISSUE.
      *         5.  ON THE FOLLOWING DAY THE ISSUE TRANSACTION WOULD
      *             CAUSE THE CORRECT ONHAND TO BE SENT.  HOWEVER THE
      *             ONHAND IN "PRAPS" OR OTHER ACCOUNTING PROGRAMS
      *             WOULD BE WRONG FOR 1 DAY.
      *      3.  ADDED A TEST MODE TO THE PROGRAM.  IF THE JCW "TEST"
      *      IS SET TO 99, NO DELETES WILL BE DONE IN DDAILYTC.  THIS
      *      WAY TRANSACTIONS NEED NOT BE REGENERATED EACH TIME THE
      *      PROGRAM IS TESTED.
      *         CIH.
      *
      *    ON JULY 8, 1985, ADDED THE FILE SEQUENCE NUMBER TO THE FIRST
      *    CONTROL RECORD OF "ABSTFILE".  FORMERLY THE SEQUENCE NUMBER
      *    WAS ONLY ON THE LAST RECORD.  CIH.
      *
      *    ON AUGUST 13, 1985, ADDED THE CUTOFF DATE TO THE
      *    "P 02" SEQUENCE COUNTER DATA ENTRY IN THE MPLTINFO
      *    DATA SET.  THIS WILL NOW GIVE THE DATE OF THE LAST
      *    CUTOFF (USED BY RECEIVING PROGRAMS FOR SPECIAL KELLY
      *    LOGIC).  CIH.
      *
      *    02/04/86.
      *      ADDED THE STR-ONORDER QUANTITY TO THE TC-999 TRANSACTION.
      *      CIH.
      *
      *C  09/21/1992      DAVE PLUM      REQUEST #6261
      *C  ADDED TC 326 TO THE SET OF VALID TRANSACTIONS.  TC 326
      *C  CONTAINS DOCK RECEIPT ACCOUNTING INFORMATION.
      *C
      *C  07FEB1994    DAVE PLUM
      *C    ADDED CALL TO THE COBOL ERROR HANDLER - MCXCBLERR.
      *C
      *C  09/12/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C    EXPAND DATE FIELD FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C    COMPUTE CENTURY FOR TRANSACTION DATE AND CUTOFF
      *C    DATE TO CHECK IF TRANSACTIONS ARE TO BE PASSED
      *C    FOR THOSE PLANTS WITH THE APPROPRIATE SWITCHES
      *C    SET TO HOLD BACK TRANSACTIONS FROM THE NEW
      *C    MONTH.  CHANGE THE DATE/TIME ON TC999 TO THE
      *C    CURRENT DATE/TIME.
      *C
      *C   1/14/97    BILL ROXBURY REQ #95-012
      *C     ADDED UPDATES TO NEW RECEIVING FILE (MCFLCSRCPT).
      *C
      *C   24JAN1997   DAVE PLUM
      *C     MODIFIED THE SPECIAL AKRON MIX CENTER LOGIC TO MORE
      *C     CLEARLY DIFFERENTIATE THE AKRON MIX CENTER FROM AKRON
      *C     PLANT 1.  BOTH OF THESE PLANTS USE "111" AS THEIR
      *C     COMPANY CODE (MPLTINFO-COMPANY), BUT THE MIX CENTER
      *C     NEEDS TO USE "11M" FOR THE CONTROL RECORDS THAT ARE
      *C     WRITTEN TO THE ABSTFILE.
      *C
      *C  11/25/97    JEFF BUNGO   REQ #97-017
      *C     ADD USAGE FIELDS FOR DIRECT DELIVERY.  DD USAGE
      *C     TO BE STORED IN ADDITIONAL FIELD AND TOTAL USAGE.
      *C     STORE ISSUE USAGE CALCULATED BY TOTAL USAGE - DD USAGE.
      *C
      *C  27JAN1998   DAVE PLUM
      *C     REVISED LOGIC FOR THE RECEIVED YESTERDAY FILE TO NOT
      *C     PROCESS RECEIPTS FOR NON-CODED ITEMS (NON-STR).  ALSO
      *C     ADDED TRANSACTIONS 523, 524, 623, AND 624 TO THE SET OF
      *C     DOCK RECEIPT TRANSACTIONS PROCESSED TO OBTAIN RECEIVED
      *C     YESTERDAY DATA.
      *C
      *C  29JAN1998   BILL ROXBURY
      *C     ADDED PROCESSING TO PERFORM THE ACTUAL UPDATING OF THE
      *C     RECEIPTS FILE USING THE RECEIVED YESTERDAY FILE RECORDS.
      *C
DP9802*C  02FEB1998   DAVE PLUM
DP9802*C     ADDED ADDITIONAL LOGIC FOR TRANSACTIONS 354, 523, 524,
DP9802*C     623, AND 624.
      *C*************  END OF COMMENTS SECTION  **********************

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.        IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.        IBM-AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.          LOCAL-DATA IS LOCAL-DATA-AREA.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT ABST-FILE  ASSIGN      TO  DISK-ABSTFILE.
           SELECT USED-YEST-FILE ASSIGN  TO  DISK-USYESFIL.
           SELECT RECD-YEST-FILE ASSIGN  TO  DISK-RECDYSFIL.
           SELECT TC-999-IN-FILE ASSIGN  TO  DISK-TC999IN.
           SELECT TC-999-OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO  DISK-TC999OUT.
           SELECT SORT-FILE ASSIGN       TO  DISK-SORT.

           SELECT MPLTINFO-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DDAILYTC-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT USAGEFIL-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCSUSAG
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT RECEIPTFIL-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCSRCPT
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-I
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.

       FD  ABST-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD
           RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS
           DATA RECORD IS ABST-RCD.
